  "result": "I added `click.KeyValue` and its tests. The full suite passes (1915 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\n**What changed:**\n- **`src/click/types.py`**: new `KeyValue(ParamType[tuple[str, str]])`. It splits on the first `=`, so `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`. A missing `=` or an empty key fails with `\"... is not a valid key=value pair.\"`. An empty value like `a=` is accepted. A value that is already a tuple passes through unchanged.\n- **`src/click/__init__.py`**: exports `KeyValue`.\n- **`docs/api.md`, `docs/parameter-types.md`**: autoclass entries.\n- **`CHANGES.md`**: entry under a new \"Version 8.6.0 / Unreleased\" heading.\n- **`tests/test_types.py`**: 9 new tests covering valid inputs, the error cases, tuple passthrough, and an end-to-end `--set` option with `multiple=True`.\n\n**Deviations from the plan:**\n- The changelog is `CHANGES.md`, not `CHANGES.rst`.\n- The version is 8.6.0, since 8.5.0 is already released. The plan didn't name a version.\n\nNothing is committed. I didn't run linters or mypy.",
